      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "to determine the reliability and the concurrent validity of the Spineangel lumbo-pelvic postural monitoring device."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "the dynamic lumbo-pelvic posture of 25 participants was simultaneously monitored by the Spineangel and Fastrak devices. Participants performed six different functional tasks in random order. Within-task, within-session and between-day intraclass correlation coefficients (ICC(3,1), ICC(3,5), ICC(2,5), respectively) reliability were calculated for Spineangel measurements. Concurrent validity of the Spineangel was assessed by means of a Bland and Altman plot and by means of Pearson's correlation coefficient and paired t-test."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "within-task, within-session and between-day ICC for the Spineangel were found to be excellent (>0.93). The Spineangel and Fastrak pelvic measurements were found to have a good correlation (R = 0.77)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "the Spineangel is a reliable and valid device for monitoring general lumbo-pelvic movements when clipped on the belt or waistband of workers' clothing during various occupational activities."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "PRACTITIONER SUMMARY",
          "content": "The Spineangel can be used for assessing lumbo-pelvic posture during work or daily-life activities. This device was found to provide reliable and valid measurements for lumbo-pelvic movements. Further research is required to determine whether the use of this device is clinically relevant for patients presenting with low back pain."
        }
      ]},
